VARIANTS:
  - primary: date +%s%N (nanosecond timestamp)
  - fallback 1: echo $RANDOM$RANDOM (bash random)
  - fallback 2: erlang:unique_integer() (Erlang unique int)

INVARIANTS:
  - Must generate unique IDs for workspace isolation
  - IDs must be collision-resistant
  - Failure modes should be explicit

CURRENT BROKEN CODE (worktree.gleam:253-265):
  fn generate_unique_id() -> String {
    case process.run_command("date", ["+%s%N"], ".") {
      Ok(process.Success(timestamp, _, _)) ->
        timestamp |> string.trim |> string.slice(unique_id_offset, unique_id_length)
      _ ->
        case process.run_command("sh", ["-c", "echo $RANDOM$RANDOM"], ".") {
          Ok(process.Success(rand, _, _)) -> string.trim(rand)
          _ -> int.to_string(int.absolute_value(erlang_unique_integer()))
        }
    }
  }

ISSUES:
  1. string.slice may fail if timestamp too short (single-digit nanoseconds)
  2. $RANDOM$RANDOM gives 4-10 digits, inconsistent length
  3. No validation of ID uniqueness
  4. Silent fallback - no logging when primary fails
  5. No error if ALL strategies fail

HAPPY PATH (after fix):
  - date +%s%N works -> 8-char ID extracted safely
  - Fallback to Erlang with explicit logging
  - Clear error if all fail

UNHAPPY PATH:
  - date command not available -> logged, fallback tried
  - All strategies fail -> explicit Error

MANUAL TEST:
  1. factory new -s test-id1; factory new -s test-id2; factory new -s test-id3
  2. ls .factory-workspaces/ (verify unique IDs)
  3. Test with date unavailable: PATH="" factory new -s test-no-date
  4. Should use fallback, log warning

FILES:
  - src/worktree.gleam:253-265 (generate_unique_id)
  - src/worktree.gleam:246-248 (unique_id_offset, unique_id_length constants)

CODE EXAMPLE (FIX):
  fn generate_unique_id() -> Result(String, String) {
    try_timestamp()
    |> result.lazy_error(fn(_) {
      logging.log(logging.Warn, "date command failed, using random fallback", dict.new())
      try_random()
    })
    |> result.lazy_error(fn(_) {
      logging.log(logging.Warn, "bash random failed, using Erlang fallback", dict.new())
      Ok(erlang_fallback())
    })
  }

  fn try_timestamp() -> Result(String, String) {
    use result <- result.try(process.run_command("date", ["+%s%N"], "."))
    case result {
      process.Success(ts, _, 0) -> {
        let trimmed = string.trim(ts)
        case string.length(trimmed) >= unique_id_offset + unique_id_length {
          True -> Ok(string.slice(trimmed, unique_id_offset, unique_id_length))
          False -> Error("timestamp too short")
        }
      }
      _ -> Error("date command failed")
    }
  }

  fn try_random() -> Result(String, String) {
    use result <- result.try(process.run_command("sh", ["-c", "echo $RANDOM$RANDOM"], "."))
    case result {
      process.Success(rand, _, 0) -> Ok(string.trim(rand))
      _ -> Error("random generation failed")
    }
  }

  fn erlang_fallback() -> String {
    int.to_string(int.absolute_value(erlang_unique_integer()))
  }
